# B09: E-Commerce Order Lifecycle Finite State Machine (`OrderFsm`)

This module implements an e-commerce order state machine (`OrderStateMachine`) governing the following valid state transitions:
- `0 (Created)` $\rightarrow$ `1 (Paid)` or `4 (Cancelled)`
- `1 (Paid)` $\rightarrow$ `2 (Shipped)` or `4 (Cancelled)`
- `2 (Shipped)` $\rightarrow$ `3 (Delivered)`
- Terminal states `3 (Delivered)` and `4 (Cancelled)` cannot transition further.

Every valid state transition monotonically increments `version` (`ensures self.version == old(self.version) + 1`).

```jenny
module order_fsm

pub enum FsmError {
    InvalidTransition,
    AlreadyTerminal,
    InvalidAmount,
}

pub struct OrderStateMachine {
    pub order_id: i64,
    pub state: i32 = 0,
    pub version: usize = 1,
    pub paid_cents: i64 = 0,

    invariant {
        self.state >= 0 && self.state <= 4
        self.version >= 1
        self.paid_cents >= 0
    }
}

impl OrderStateMachine {
    pub fn new(order_id: i64) -> OrderStateMachine
        ensures result.state == 0
        ensures result.version == 1

    pub fn pay(mut self, amount_cents: i64) -> void ! FsmError
        requires self.state == 0 else FsmError.InvalidTransition
        requires amount_cents > 0 else FsmError.InvalidAmount
        ensures self.state == 1
        ensures self.version == old(self.version) + 1

    pub fn ship(mut self) -> void ! FsmError
        requires self.state == 1 else FsmError.InvalidTransition
        ensures self.state == 2
        ensures self.version == old(self.version) + 1

    pub fn deliver(mut self) -> void ! FsmError
        requires self.state == 2 else FsmError.InvalidTransition
        ensures self.state == 3
        ensures self.version == old(self.version) + 1

    pub fn cancel(mut self) -> void ! FsmError
        requires self.state == 0 || self.state == 1 else FsmError.AlreadyTerminal
        ensures self.state == 4
        ensures self.version == old(self.version) + 1
}

@example("EX-B09-01: valid lifecycle Created -> Paid -> Shipped -> Delivered") {
    var fsm = OrderStateMachine.new(9001)
    assert(fsm.state == 0)

    fsm.pay(4500)!
    assert(fsm.state == 1)
    assert(fsm.version == 2)
    assert(fsm.paid_cents == 4500)

    fsm.ship()!
    assert(fsm.state == 2)
    assert(fsm.version == 3)

    fsm.deliver()!
    assert(fsm.state == 3)
    assert(fsm.version == 4)
}

@example("EX-B09-02: reject illegal backward transition and cancel after ship") {
    var fsm = OrderStateMachine.new(9002)
    val ship_early = fsm.ship()
    assert(ship_early is FsmError.InvalidTransition)

    fsm.pay(3000)!
    fsm.ship()!

    val cancel_late = fsm.cancel()
    assert(cancel_late is FsmError.AlreadyTerminal)
    assert(fsm.state == 2)
}
```
